    "verbatim_text": "So log into your Onshape and open a new document and first we're going to start a sketch on the top plane. And click OK. So what I'd like to do first is I get an idea of what the profile looks like. So it's got this little U-shape, uh, it's got a thin wall, and it's got a little sort of clip hook kind of thing there. And what I'll do is I'll just sort of draw that out using lines. So there's a few ways you can do it. I think what I'll do is I will draw the outline, then offset it into the middle, and then add the little tooth. So always think about what you're going to do before you start drawing. So, line, line, line, line, line, line, escape. Also do remember to change your units before you start drawing. I'm working in millimeters, uh, and you can also work in inches if you prefer. Alright, so now I think it's about time to just start adding some basic dimensions in. So I'm going to work out how wide the part is. So we've got 12.5... Okay. So we got, let's say 12.6. 12.6. And overall height of... I'd say 19 millimeters. 19. And then the little lip bit that will... if I can measure it... 8.85.",
